{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left","id":27847,"title":"What to the Judges DO with relics? Why are so many still left?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-11T02:18:07-08:00","id":27847,"title":"What to the Judges DO with relics? Why are so many still left?","content":"They say that relics are the chess pieces the gods use to manipulate the world... so why would they want to take them off the board? Are they gathering power... but what for?<br /> <br /> Also - Irem was something like 5000 years ago - why are any relics left in the world? I understand inheritor cultures have made some, but really that many?<br /> <br /> My brain keeps trying to wrap itself around these bits of the world, in order to create story around them, and I can't quite make it happen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T03:25:01-08:00","id":27866,"title":"","content":"What the Arisen know is that relics they have personally delivered back to Duat (according to their memories, at least) have been returned to the world of the living. Some Arisen have even returned the same relics many times. Clearly, there is some mechanism at work there that allows the Judges to bring not just mummies (living, breathing relics), but also relics, back into the world.<br /> <br /> What the Arisen suspect, and there is some evidence to support their belief, is that the point of relics aren't their benefits, but their curses. By way of its curse, a relic distorts reality. Relics eat energy, and it is this energy that sustains the Judges. There wouldn't be much point in creating a relic if you can only use it once.<br /> <br /> Some of these questions are answered in the storyteller section of Mummy, but seeing as this is not a spoiler thread, I see no need to cover them here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T03:27:39-08:00","id":27870,"title":"","content":"Wait what?! That wasn't in the corebook was that in Guildhalls of the Deathless? That is a pretty huge revelation!<br /> <br /> What I was going to say is Irem was just a large producer of Relics, Relics occur naturally throughout the world due to the caprice of Genius/Mania/Occult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T16:37:57-08:00","id":28375,"title":"","content":"Like you said, successor cultures and individuals have occasionally created relics. Sekhem is a natural occult energy of our world and it accumulates in objects over time just on its own, creating vestiges which need to be taken to Duat. The Judges themselves have the power to create relics, too, and expect them to be returned in a...timely fashion.<br /> <br /> Don't think that the Judges are 'removing' pieces from the world; think of it more like they're playing a game of Pokemon and, in order to win their games against each other, they need to 'collect them all!'. Christian A nails it in saying the curses are the 'intended' effects. What are the Judges really doing with all of this energy? Time will tell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T17:53:40-08:00","id":28421,"title":"","content":"I read the storyteller section, and I don't remember anything about relics being returned to the world. Was it in GHotD? Did I somehow skim over it in the core book? <br /> <br /> What does it take to declare something a [spoilers] thread? This is my first post here.<br /> <br /> I like the ideas presented here, though it does beg the question: does that mean judges would want anybody /except/ their own minions to have the items, and particularly not members of the guilds that created them (since the curses have so much less effect, due to the mummy's efficient natural use of them). <br /> <br /> In which case, why would we see Mummy's always attempting to gather relics and &quot;dispose&quot; of them, instead of (at /least/ as often) going out and making sure the right relic gets into the hands of its intended victim / user?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T22:24:46-08:00","id":28544,"title":"","content":"The Judges have little to gain from their minions knowing things that undead automatons/errand boys aren't supposed to know. See also: Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T05:22:53-08:00","id":28646,"title":"","content":"Okay, but back up to the thing about relics returning. Source?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T07:46:07-08:00","id":28723,"title":"","content":"Third sentence of the first paragraph of the writeup for the Blood Coin Bell in Guildhalls, page 145.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T15:17:24-08:00","id":28960,"title":"","content":"Awesome, thanks. That's what I get for not reading the adventures. Though it seems to imply less that there's a constant treadmill of items exiting and then returning to duat, and more that <i>very occasionally</i> a judge will create a new relic specifically for the temporary use of a guildmaster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T10:15:39-08:00","id":29978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=28723#post28723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third sentence of the first paragraph of the writeup for the Blood Coin Bell in Guildhalls, page 145.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it just me, or does that seem a pretty knackered way of introducing a decently important notion into the gameline? No doubt, thanks for the citation, <b>Satchel</b>, but I'd think such a bombshell ought to have appeared... I dunno, somewhere in a rules section?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T13:35:42-08:00","id":30087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=28960#post28960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome, thanks. That's what I get for not reading the adventures. Though it seems to imply less that there's a constant treadmill of items exiting and then returning to duat, and more that <i>very occasionally</i> a judge will create a new relic specifically for the temporary use of a guildmaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and it goes with an Authors comment that it was in the book partly to show that Judges can create relics and place them into the world if they really have to. It doesn't suggest all Relics are constantly recycled into Earth just to be Descented again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T21:53:57-08:00","id":30267,"title":"","content":"Um, I don't think anyone said the Judges returned vessels to the world. All we said was that the Judges can create relics and lend them to the Arisen - nothing about 'recycling' as in bringing Relic A to Duat, it being returned to Earth, then Relic A goes back to Duat, then back again, etc.<br /> <br /> How have the Arisen not returned all vessels to Duat over 6,000 years, you ask? It's because they haven't <i>had</i> 6,000 years. In terms of actual walking activity, they've probably had a few centuries. Mummies that, frankly and I apologize for the meta-gameyness here, aren't PCs (or aren't NPCs in a campaign of PCs) probably don't wake up as often or engage in as much activity. They mostly wake up because of disturbed tombs or their cult summons them, which means their first purpose takes precedence over general relic-hunting. They also hate each other, scheming across millennia to spite one another, or try to indulge in some mortal life occasionally. There's an instinct for Mummies to hunt relics, as we humans have an instinct to eat food, but it's not what they do with <i>all</i> of their time, no more than we sit around and...um...well...you get the idea.<br /> <br /> Dammit, America, if you weren't so fat my metaphors would be better!<br /> <br /> My point is while Mummies hunt vessels and feel a natural urge to do so, they also have other matters to attend to, which become more urgent once that first purpose is accomplished because then they'll automatically succeed at their scheduled Descent rolls! This is all in addition to vessels naturally accumulating Sekhem over time as well as Judges creating relics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T01:29:00-08:00","id":30331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=30267#post30267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, I don't think anyone said the Judges returned vessels to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I was responding to Christian A saying basically exactly that, and wondering if that was said canonically somewhere. <br /> <br /> But anyway, I suspect the reason there are still so many is that they're still being created. Both the example relics (most of which come from well after the fall of Irem) and the creators of the game confirm that. So it's not like the number of relics was set at the fall of irem and eventually we're going to run out. People are still making more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T09:44:24-08:00","id":30465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=30331#post30331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, I was responding to Christian A saying basically exactly that, and wondering if that was said canonically somewhere.<br /> <br /> But anyway, I suspect the reason there are still so many is that they're still being created. Both the example relics (most of which come from well after the fall of Irem) and the creators of the game confirm that. So it's not like the number of relics was set at the fall of irem and eventually we're going to run out. People are still making more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly I was responding to Christian A saying exactly that, this isn't a very big thread so you can read all of it before making assumptions.<br /> <br /> And yeah relics frankly seem to have always been created at least as long as mankind has used items.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T10:20:34-08:00","id":30475,"title":"","content":"I took the whole Judges returning relics into the world thing from a conversation I had with Michael Goodwin; in addition to the Guildhalls quote. Might not actually have made it into the final books, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T13:54:50-08:00","id":30567,"title":"","content":"Huh. I'd be really really interested in that conversation. It seems like there's a lot of the, like...basic metaphysics of the setting that the mummy creators are holding back, which makes me wonder why they bothered separating out the storyteller section if they were going to consciously keep the storytellers in the dark as well.<br /> <br /> I criticize because I love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T03:43:49-08:00","id":32270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=30267#post30267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How have the Arisen not returned all vessels to Duat over 6,000 years, you ask? It's because they haven't <i>had</i> 6,000 years. In terms of actual walking activity, they've probably had a few centuries. . . They mostly wake up because of disturbed tombs or their cult summons them, which means their first purpose takes precedence over general relic-hunting. They also hate each other, scheming across millennia to spite one another, or try to indulge in some mortal life occasionally. There's an instinct for Mummies to hunt relics, as we humans have an instinct to eat food, but it's not what they do with <i>all</i> of their time, no more than we sit around and...um...well...you get the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you're proposing that:<br /> 1) They're not awake that much<br /> 2) They don't care that much<br /> 3) They get in each other's way a lot<br /> <br /> It seems they should be awake a fair bit, though: most Mummy's have some vessel to help return them (as I recall), and with a vessel their cult can return them fairly frequently - on the order of months, if they went at the soonest. Even if they do complete their first purpose immediately, they have the better part of a year to stay awake. <br /> <br /> Stated demographics establish at least a &quot;Few thousand&quot; active Mummies at present, yes? Enough to have a critical mass for a worldwide culture of Guilds. Thousands of Mummies, active for one year out of every - what? 5? 10? An average as high as 25 would mean you'd start losing cult continuity as nobody actually knew how to wake their 'protector' anymore. While that surely happens, it seems unlikely that it would be the norm. Plus the general Sothic awakenings.<br /> <br /> Plus, recovery of a Relic generally counts, if not as their first purpose, at least a power bump for having pleased the Judges - since it was established that they really do want their relics back a whole lot, 'like parents would want lost children'. Which seems pretty motivating to me. And even if they schemed to deny the other guy the chance to recover some relic, they'd still want to do it themselves, since it gets them credit with their own boss. While that may end up in lost opportunities sometimes, given the Judges really REALLY want those relics, I doubt it could be too often, or else somebody would get smacked down.<br /> <br /> All of which leads to the conclusion of thousands of Mummy-work-years active and motivated to recover artifacts.<br /> <br /> All of which leads to some mixture of the following:<br /> 1) Quite a lot of relics have been made over time<br /> 2) Quite a lot of relics have been returned over time<br /> 3) Mummies aren't very good at getting / keeping relics. <br /> <br /> Since #3 doesn't seem supported by the rules or story, it would seem some combination of 1 and 2 are the most likely results.<br /> <br /> .... Which brings me back to my starting question: WHY do the Judges want to eat the relics so much? If the relics are chess pieces, why take them off the board? Are they capturing the other guy's pieces, in order to send back a relic to their advantage? Does that mean the sum of relics in the world is a zero sum game, which is why the Judges think of /all/ relics as their property, because even if they're not from Irem, they're powered by legacy sekhem which has been recycled? Or is the world constantly creating new relics on its own, and the Judges want them sent to Duat to feed their own appetites? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mummies that, frankly and I apologize for the meta-gameyness here, aren't PCs (or aren't NPCs in a campaign of PCs) probably don't wake up as often or engage in as much activity. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the PCs haven't even been PCs for their whole lives. If they're expected to believe that relic-acquisition is a thing they should do as a Mummy, there should be some internally consistent, believable reason (even if their characters aren't immediately privy to it) why that's a problem which keeps popping up and needs solving.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T05:33:28-08:00","id":32312,"title":"","content":"Just because a cult <i>can</i> awaken its Mummy doesn't mean it <i>should</i>; see Frivolous Awakenings on pg 26 of the core, as well as All Work and No Play on the opposite page (and since Arisen lose a Memory dot every time they complete a Descent - <i>unless they rise from tomb disturbance</i> - then I'm sure quite a few have made it clear to their cults to Please Not Disturb unless very, very important). I'm not meaning to split hairs. Vessel collection is an important aspect of Mummy existence but it's not the only aspect.<br /> <br /> Anyway. I don't know. Similar to your last suggestion, I envisioned the Judges being these ghastly parasites which siphon out the various energies of our living world because that's what they feed on. Maybe one day we'll get a more concrete answer.<br /> <br /> Maybe not; maybe this is an aspect left intentionally vague to please all the people who think Mummy's background is too meta-plotty <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T06:41:14-08:00","id":32350,"title":"","content":"Thousands of Active Mummies? What? The impression I have is that likely less then a 1000 Arisen even exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T07:05:29-08:00","id":32366,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">Around 6000, according to Colin (as he mentioned on Facebook in the dice problems group). Boy, those Shan'iatu must have been busy killing people and making them their undying servants.<br /> <br /> It is important to remember, however, that, at any given time, most mummies are dead. Also, they tend to find themselves in cities where other mummies are, drawn there by kepher and Fate - there is no real relationship between population and mummy population; the needs of Fate (read: the Storyteller) are more important.<br /> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:14:39-08:00","id":33395,"title":"","content":"Wow that's insanely more then I thought.<br /> <br /> Also considering the impression was that possibly only some of the people they mummified trying to create the Arisen actually successfully Arose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:27:00-08:00","id":33405,"title":"","content":"Well also remember that Ancient Egypt, one of the inheritor empires, had a tenure of multiple thousands of years. Irem probably lasted <i>longer</i>. So they had a lot of time to get as many mummies going as they wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:56:42-08:00","id":33436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=33405#post33405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well also remember that Ancient Egypt, one of the inheritor empires, had a tenure of multiple thousands of years. Irem probably lasted <i>longer</i>. So they had a lot of time to get as many mummies going as they wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, isn't the range of Arisen Sothic Turns something like a full century or two? That's thirty to sixty successfully-made mummies per year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T15:10:01-08:00","id":33443,"title":"","content":"Where exactly does it say that about the Sothic turn?<br /> <br /> The rulebook says that the period when mummies arise en masse is called the Sothic Turn and happens every 1,461 years (give or take a decade or three), so I always assumed the all mummies awoke around the same time. The only way you could say the Turn lasts centuries is that Mummies are off the clock when at Sekhem 1, so they can theoretically stay awake indefinately when on the Sothic turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T15:15:54-08:00","id":33450,"title":"","content":"It says somewhere in the first chapter (I forget exactly where) that the Sothic Arising is cycled around when each individual mummy was made, so the actual wake-up dates are spread out over a fair amount of time, but clumped around the dates given for the sothic turns. I forget what the interval was, but a century or two sounds right. Some will always wake up early, some will always and forever be late to the party.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T15:17:37-08:00","id":33451,"title":"","content":"Here we go, page 21, &quot;The Sothic Wheel&quot;:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;The Shan\u2019iatu incorporated these celestial energies into the Rite of Return, though these dynamics are tied to the day of the Arisen\u2019s first death, rather than to Sirius, itself. Nevertheless, the sorcerer-priests appear to have created most of the Arisen on or within a century or so of Sirius\u2019 natural cycle.&quot;</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:01:02-08:00","id":33487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=33451#post33451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here we go, page 21, &quot;The Sothic Wheel&quot;:<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\">&quot;The Shan\u2019iatu incorporated these celestial energies into the Rite of Return, though these dynamics are tied to the day of the Arisen\u2019s first death, rather than to Sirius, itself. Nevertheless, the sorcerer-priests appear to have created most of the Arisen on or within a century or so of Sirius\u2019 natural cycle.&quot;</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This always implied to me that Irem only lasted as a distinct empire for a century or two. My impression was that the scorpion priests marched in, created an empire on the quick, and - just as their unnaturally extended lifespans were wearing out, consumed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T17:59:27-08:00","id":33576,"title":"","content":"Thats another secret I wish had been included in the storyteller section. The duration of the empire is fairly unclear. It could've been as short as centuries or longer than a sothic turn. I personally assumed that is rose one sothic cycle, then fell the next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T00:21:08-08:00","id":33739,"title":"","content":"My pet Head Canon. (That AFAIK isn't contradicted, but may not have been intendedd to be a story teller option),<br /> is that Duat, and the whole mummy ecosystem, is all one giant, ancient piece of infrastructure for the God Machine.<br /> Designed to locate and retrieve Relics, for its use.<br /> <br /> The God Machine has many uses for Magical objects, be they relics, artefacts, tokens or fetishes.<br /> The Tomb of the Butterfly, was full of artefacts.<br /> I like to think that alot of infrastructure draws power from magic items, to run it's preprocessors.<br /> <br /> So where are the relics going?<br /> They are becoming part of infrastructure.<br /> The godmachine pulls them out of duat, as needed and brings them back to it's infrastructure set-ups, on this plain or others.<br /> <br /> If relics are reappear<br /> well sometimes infrastucture is destroyed (or dismantled and parts lost in transit).<br /> <br /> <br /> If i was ever to use it in play I would prob make some kind a of acronym for I.S.S.A.M or D.U.A.T,<br /> meaning Super Long Term Artefact Discovery and Retrieval Strategy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1699-oxinabox","name":"oxinabox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T01:01:07-08:00","id":33749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>oxinabox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=33739#post33739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My pet Head Canon. (That AFAIK isn't contradicted, but may not have been intendedd to be a story teller option),<br /> is that Duat, and the whole mummy ecosystem, is all one giant, ancient piece of infrastructure for the God Machine.<br /> Designed to locate and retrieve Relics, for its use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I like it the other way around - the God Machine is one giant relic left over from the Nameless Empire. Maybe they left it behind, to help ensure the world stayed in the shape of their wishes - maybe it grew, tumorously from something stolen, forgotten or abandoned, still trying to build a world in the image of its Creators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T08:35:16-08:00","id":33884,"title":"","content":"Although the God-machine isn't present in my campaign, I have wondered how one might integrate it into Mummy.<br /> <br /> Its job, in part, is to collect occult energy, and that's what Sekhem is. Tombs and their relic-based Lifeweb sound a lot like infrastructure. I envision it not liking any Mummies, though; coming back from the dead over and over again and wielding antediluvian Utterances just isn't part of its Grand Design.<br /> <br /> While we're off-topic can I say that, in my campaign, the Shan'iatu are canonically extra-terrestrials? How that fits into the God-machine I have no idea. How that fits into a demonic underworld I have no idea","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T12:58:13-08:00","id":34028,"title":"","content":"The beauty of a horror/mystery game is, you don't have to have answers to these questions. The game doesn't necessarily benefit from answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T13:42:40-08:00","id":34057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/27847-what-to-the-judges-do-with-relics-why-are-so-many-still-left?p=34028#post34028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beauty of a horror/mystery game is, you don't have to have answers to these questions. The game doesn't necessarily benefit from answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think the ST, at least, should have some idea why things are happening.<br /> <br /> The compelling aspect of mystery and horror stories begins with being believable enough to be scary and having a world where mysteries /can/ be investigated and useful knowledge acquired, even if not everything ends up with a definitive answer. Games where I feel the ST is just throwing shit at us to make our lives difficult aren't mysterious or scary, though they can be fun exercises in tactics and strategy.<br /> <br /> If I'm just supposed to gather [doodads] because [doodad gathering] gets me [points], then that's a much different game than if I'm tasked with stealing the Windsor Reed from Lu Shan, world famous flutist (before it drives him and everybody in earshot mad), in order to return it to Duat to further plans I'm not really privy to, but the ST seems a bit gleeful every time I advance. Maybe the reason why never becomes part of my story, but there should still BE some reason, lurking in shadows left unexplored. <br /> <br /> I'm not saying the ST needs to know everything in the universe before running a game, but I do think that if you're presenting something as important, there should be some reason why it's important. It's not a mystery unless there are clues. <br /> <br /> Which is why this question bothers me so much - how can there be so many left after all this time? I guess the concept that some are returned and enough are made to keep it a viable concern is sufficient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1627-xavieram","name":"XavierAM","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-20T16:37:03-08:00","id":34169,"title":"","content":"I guess I kind of agree. Not every core-book answers every question, though, either so let's hope the upcoming supplements answer some questions!<br /> <br /> Although I am privy to Christian A's statement. For now, for me at least, it's enough to know the Judges want them. That's part of the experience for an Arisen who will eventually rebel one day, &quot;Why do the Judges want these relics? I don't even know! I've been running around doing some meaningless task for centuries and I don't know why! You know what?! Screw them!&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, the GM can still know why the Judges want them. Hell, the player could as well if they can divorce it from character knowledge. Wasn't that the whole purpose of separating our core into two sections? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}